{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/885551-questions-about-needle-gift-facet","id":885551,"title":"Questions about Needle Gift Facet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-08T11:56:11-07:00","id":885551,"title":"Questions about Needle Gift Facet","content":"I was torn over the Needle Gift Facet. On the surface it seems sort of simple, you hide a piece of information from someone. But it has a nice duration of one month, can include basically any information you have a physical version of, and activates spirits to conceal any physical copies of the information. It's possible to find the information again, but with a penalty based on the Renown of the Facet.<br /> <br /> Anyways I was wondering if anyone had taken advantage of it or just sees interesting ways to use the facet. Does it have to be information they don't have yet, like a book on werewolf lore that you had a copy of? I suppose I could see it used a lot for helping the 'Masquerade,' by concealing evidence until you can eliminate the actual witness, for those who don't have Veil.<br /> <br /> Just to get this out of the way here's the primary and success write-ups.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Uratha chooses a single piece of information that he is in the presence of a copy of, and the prey from which it will be concealed. It may be a fact, a specific book, a map, or a timetable for a local public transit - anything is fair game.<br /> ...<br /> Success: The prey loses any copy of the hidden information that she has on her person; she drops it without noticing, manages to mislay it, or finds the file on her computer has been corrupted. If the prey seeks the hidden information, spiritual activity and random happenstance conspire against her. All dice pools to reveal or discover the knowledge in question suffer a penalty equal to the Uratha's Cunning, and research times are doubled. Humans find they can't quite remember exactly where the house was, or the relevant books in a library are all out of stock at the moment. </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T12:26:46-07:00","id":885582,"title":"","content":"I actually used it last session. A rival pack acquired a detailed summoning ritual, that forces the summoned spirit to obey. Naturally, they were going to summon our totem, and use it against us. I Needle'd it away, and now we're planning our counter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:47:03-07:00","id":885657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/885551-questions-about-needle-gift-facet?p=885582#post885582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually used it last session. A rival pack acquired a detailed summoning ritual, that forces the summoned spirit to obey. Naturally, they were going to summon our totem, and use it against us. I Needle'd it away, and now we're planning our counter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like fun!<br /> <br /> A question, though. Did they learn the ritual, or have it on a parchment or something? Because while the gift says you can hide any information, including 'a fact,' it's unclear to me if you can hide knowledge they actually know already.<br /> <br /> For instance if you're pulled over and a cop gets your license and name from it, can you use your license to hide your name from her <i>after s</i>he's learned it? Or would you only be able to use it on, say, the ticket she filled out so she wouldn't be able to find a copy of it, so she would have no hard evidence of your location and name, just her memories of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:59:00-07:00","id":885670,"title":"","content":"Needle doesn't let you wipe memory, just instances of the information; so if the cop notes down your license and name, you can then use Needle to wipe it off her ticket and leave her just with memory that it happened but no hard evidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:09:36-07:00","id":885682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/885551-questions-about-needle-gift-facet?p=885670#post885670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Needle doesn't let you wipe memory, just instances of the information; so if the cop notes down your license and name, you can then use Needle to wipe it off her ticket and leave her just with memory that it happened but no hard evidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was something like that. Presumably you could get a fetish to alter it to encompass the mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}